IMPORT prelude

-- Electronic Transactions Act 1999 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- whether a click, an email or a scan is enough.
--
-- SEAT: the contracting party -- "Is an electronic signature and a click-through enough to meet a Commonwealth law's
-- requirement for writing, a signature, production or retention of a document? When is what I send taken to be sent and
-- received? Am I bound by something sent in my name? Is a website's price list an offer? Can I take back a typing
-- error?". Where the Act hands a judgment to someone else (whether a method was "as reliable as appropriate"; whether a
-- State law is "in terms substantially the same as" Part 2A), it is asked as a fact, and the answer is conditional on it.
--
-- THIS IS THE COMMONWEALTH ACT. Western Australia has its own Electronic Transactions Act 2011 (deposited at
-- subjects/au/wa/electronic-transactions-act-2011, NOT encoded here). Sections 8-15 of this Act apply only "for the
-- purposes of a law of the Commonwealth"; a requirement under a WA law (or the general law of contract in WA) is the WA
-- Act's business, not this one's.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 5(1) (consent, electronic communication, automated message system, Commonwealth entity, as used);
-- s 7A (exemptions under the regulations, as an input); s 7B(1) (court and tribunal practice and procedure); s 9(1), (5)
-- (writing); s 10(1), (3) (signature); s 11(1), (3), (5) and Schedule 1 (production of a document; migration and
-- citizenship documents exempt); s 12(1), (2), (4) (recording and retention); s 14(1) (time of dispatch); s 14A(1), (2)
-- (time of receipt); s 15(1), (2) (attribution); s 15A(2) and s 17(3) (when Part 2A applies); s 15B (invitation to treat);
-- s 15C (automated contracts); s 15D(2), (3) (input errors).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 4 (register id C2026C00011), compilation date 5 December 2025, including amendments up to Act
-- No. 73, 2025, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00553.txt (retrieved 13 October 2026).
-- NOT DEPOSITED: the Electronic Transactions Regulations (the laws, transactions and matters exempted under s 7A, and any
-- data-storage-device requirement under s 12). Each is an input here: "the regulations exempt it" and "any data storage
-- device the regulations require was used". The encoding cannot say which laws the regulations exempt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 9(2), s 10(2), s 11(2), (4), (6), s 12(6) (permissions, laws with their own IT rules, copyright);
-- s 7B(2) (Evidence Act unaffected); s 8 beyond its words being carried into the answers; s 14(2), s 14A(3), s 14B
-- (place of dispatch and receipt); s 15(5); s 15E (applying ss 8, 14-14B to contracts of their own force) and s 15F;
-- s 15D(4) (the consequences of a withdrawal, left to "any applicable rule of law"); ss 1-4, 6, 7, 16, 17(1), (2), (4)
-- (machinery and transitional). Whether a click forms a contract at all is the general law of contract, not this Act.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Electronic Transactions Act 1999 -- from the seat of the contracting party`

-- s 5(1): a "Commonwealth entity" is a Minister, an officer or employee of the Commonwealth, an office-holder under a law
-- of the Commonwealth, or an authority of the Commonwealth or its employee. ss 9-11 set different conditions depending on
-- whether the information goes to such an entity (its IT and verification rules) or to anyone else (their consent).
DECLARE `Who it goes to` IS ONE OF
    `a Commonwealth entity, or someone acting for one`
    `anyone else`

-- The legal requirement I want to meet electronically. Every field is something I can say about it, except the
-- regulations' exemption, which is asked because the regulations are not deposited.
DECLARE `The requirement` HAS
    `it is imposed by a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the regulations exempt this law, transaction or matter from the section` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is part of the practice and procedure of a court or tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it goes to` IS A `Who it goes to`
    `the document is for a visa, deportation or citizenship matter listed in Schedule 1` IS A BOOLEAN

-- What I did electronically to meet it. One flag is a judgment (the reliability of a signing method, s 10(1)(b)(i)).
DECLARE `What I did` HAS
    `I used an electronic communication` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was reasonable to expect the information to stay readily accessible for later reference` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the entity's information technology requirements were met, or it set none` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the entity's receipt-verification requirement was met, or it set none` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the recipient consented, expressly or by conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the method identifies me and shows my intention about the information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the method was as reliable as appropriate for the purpose, in all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the method is proven in fact to have identified me and shown my intention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the electronic form was made by a method that reliably assures the integrity of the information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `any data storage device the regulations require was used` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I also keep enough to identify its origin, destination and times sent and received` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Every Division 2 question gets one of these answers.
DECLARE `Answer` IS ONE OF
    `met electronically`
    `not met electronically: a condition of the section is not satisfied`
    `the Act does not apply: the requirement is not under a law of the Commonwealth`
    `the Act does not apply: the regulations exempt it (s 7A)`
    `the Act does not apply: court or tribunal practice and procedure (s 7B(1))`
    `the Act does not apply: a Schedule 1 migration or citizenship document (s 11(5))`

§§ `ss 7A, 7B -- does Division 2 reach my requirement at all`

-- ss 9-12: each begins "If, under a law of the Commonwealth, ...". s 7A(1)-(2): "The regulations may provide that all or
-- specified provisions of this Act do not apply" to specified transactions, requirements or laws. s 7B(1): "Part 2A and
-- Division 2 of Part 2 do not apply to the practice and procedure of a court or tribunal."
-- (Returns `met electronically` as the "reached" answer only internally; the section questions then test their own limbs.)
GIVEN `the requirement` IS A `The requirement`
GIVETH AN `Answer`
DECIDE `Why Division 2 does not reach it` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the requirement`'s `it is imposed by a law of the Commonwealth`)
            THEN `the Act does not apply: the requirement is not under a law of the Commonwealth`
        IF `the requirement`'s `the regulations exempt this law, transaction or matter from the section`
            THEN `the Act does not apply: the regulations exempt it (s 7A)`
        IF `the requirement`'s `it is part of the practice and procedure of a court or tribunal`
            THEN `the Act does not apply: court or tribunal practice and procedure (s 7B(1))`
        OTHERWISE `met electronically`

GIVEN `the requirement` IS A `The requirement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Division 2 reaches it` IF
    `Why Division 2 does not reach it` `the requirement` EQUALS `met electronically`

-- The paragraphs that turn on who receives it: (b)-(c) for a Commonwealth entity (its IT requirements, its verification
-- of receipt), (d) for anyone else (their consent; s 5(1): "consent includes consent that can reasonably be inferred from
-- the conduct of the person concerned").
GIVEN `the requirement` IS A `The requirement`
      `what I did` IS A `What I did`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `The recipient's conditions are met` IF
    CONSIDER `the requirement`'s `it goes to`
    WHEN `a Commonwealth entity, or someone acting for one` THEN
            `what I did`'s `the entity's information technology requirements were met, or it set none`
        AND `what I did`'s `the entity's receipt-verification requirement was met, or it set none`
    WHEN `anyone else` THEN `what I did`'s `the recipient consented, expressly or by conduct`

GIVEN `the requirement` IS A `The requirement`
      `limbs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Answer`
DECIDE `Answer the section` IS
    IF `Division 2 reaches it` `the requirement`
    THEN IF `limbs` THEN `met electronically` ELSE `not met electronically: a condition of the section is not satisfied`
    ELSE `Why Division 2 does not reach it` `the requirement`

§§ `s 9 -- writing`

-- s 9(1): "If, under a law of the Commonwealth, a person is required to give information in writing, that requirement is
-- taken to have been met if the person gives the information by means of an electronic communication, where: (a) in all
-- cases--at the time the information was given, it was reasonable to expect that the information would be readily
-- accessible so as to be useable for subsequent reference; and (b)" a Commonwealth entity's IT requirements, "(c)" its
-- verification of receipt, "(d)" for anyone else, "the person to whom the information is required to be given consents".
-- s 9(5): giving information includes making an application, lodging a claim or return, giving a notification, lodging an
-- objection, and so on.
@export Can I meet a Commonwealth law's requirement to give information in writing by email, web form or other electronic communication (s 9(1))?
GIVEN `the requirement` IS A `The requirement` @desc The requirement to give information in writing, and who it goes to
      `what I did` IS A `What I did` @desc How you gave the information electronically
GIVETH AN `Answer`
DECIDE `Can I meet the writing requirement electronically` IS
    `Answer the section` `the requirement`
        (    `what I did`'s `I used an electronic communication`
         AND `what I did`'s `it was reasonable to expect the information to stay readily accessible for later reference`
         AND `The recipient's conditions are met` `the requirement` `what I did`)

§§ `s 10 -- signature`

-- s 10(1): "If, under a law of the Commonwealth, the signature of a person is required, that requirement is taken to have
-- been met in relation to an electronic communication if: (a) in all cases--a method is used to identify the person and
-- to indicate the person's intention in respect of the information communicated; and (b) in all cases--the method used
-- was either: (i) as reliable as appropriate for the purpose ..., in the light of all the circumstances, including any
-- relevant agreement; or (ii) proven in fact to have fulfilled the functions described in paragraph (a) ...; and (c)" a
-- Commonwealth entity's IT requirements for the method; "(d)" for anyone else, that person "consents to that requirement
-- being met by way of the use of the method". s 10(3): a law that "provides consequences for the absence of a signature"
-- counts as requiring one. (A click on "I agree" while logged in is such a method, if it identifies me and shows my
-- intention; whether it was reliable enough is the judgment of (b)(i), asked as a fact.)
@export Is an electronic signature or a click-through enough to meet a Commonwealth law's requirement for my signature (s 10(1))?
GIVEN `the requirement` IS A `The requirement` @desc The signature requirement, and who the signature goes to
      `what I did` IS A `What I did` @desc The electronic method you used to sign
GIVETH AN `Answer`
DECIDE `Can I meet the signature requirement electronically` IS
    `Answer the section` `the requirement`
        (    `what I did`'s `I used an electronic communication`
         AND `what I did`'s `the method identifies me and shows my intention about the information`
         AND (   `what I did`'s `the method was as reliable as appropriate for the purpose, in all the circumstances`
              OR `what I did`'s `the method is proven in fact to have identified me and shown my intention`)
         AND (CONSIDER `the requirement`'s `it goes to`
              WHEN `a Commonwealth entity, or someone acting for one`
                  THEN `what I did`'s `the entity's information technology requirements were met, or it set none`
              WHEN `anyone else` THEN `what I did`'s `the recipient consented, expressly or by conduct`))

§§ `s 11 and Schedule 1 -- production of a document`

-- s 11(1): a requirement "to produce a document that is in the form of paper, an article or other material" is met by
-- producing "by means of an electronic communication, an electronic form of the document, where: (a) ... the method of
-- generating the electronic form of the document provided a reliable means of assuring the maintenance of the integrity of
-- the information contained in the document; and (b)" readily accessible for later reference; "(c)-(d)" a Commonwealth
-- entity's IT and verification requirements; "(e)" for anyone else, their consent.
-- s 11(3): integrity is maintained "if, and only if, the information has remained complete and unaltered, apart from: (a)
-- the addition of any endorsement; or (b) any immaterial change; which arises in the normal course of communication,
-- storage or display" (folded into the integrity flag).
-- s 11(5) and Schedule 1 cll 1-2: "Section 11 does not apply to a document required or permitted to be produced in
-- connection with" visa applications, grants and cancellations, deportation, unlawful non-citizens, and citizenship
-- (whether a person is a citizen, registration, approval, renunciation, revocation, the citizenship register).
@export Can I meet a Commonwealth law's requirement to produce a paper document by sending a scan or other electronic form of it (s 11(1), Schedule 1)?
GIVEN `the requirement` IS A `The requirement` @desc The requirement to produce a document, and who it goes to
      `what I did` IS A `What I did` @desc How you made and sent the electronic form
GIVETH AN `Answer`
DECIDE `Can I meet the production requirement electronically` IS
    IF (`Division 2 reaches it` `the requirement`)
       AND `the requirement`'s `the document is for a visa, deportation or citizenship matter listed in Schedule 1`
    THEN `the Act does not apply: a Schedule 1 migration or citizenship document (s 11(5))`
    ELSE `Answer the section` `the requirement`
              (    `what I did`'s `I used an electronic communication`
               AND `what I did`'s `the electronic form was made by a method that reliably assures the integrity of the information`
               AND `what I did`'s `it was reasonable to expect the information to stay readily accessible for later reference`
               AND `The recipient's conditions are met` `the requirement` `what I did`)

§§ `s 12 -- recording and retention`

-- s 12(1): a requirement "to record information in writing" is met "if the person records the information in electronic
-- form, where: (a) ... it was reasonable to expect that the information would be readily accessible so as to be useable
-- for subsequent reference; and (b) if the regulations require that the information be recorded, in electronic form, on a
-- particular kind of data storage device--that requirement has been met."
@export Can I meet a Commonwealth law's requirement to record information in writing by recording it electronically (s 12(1))?
GIVEN `the requirement` IS A `The requirement` @desc The requirement to record information
      `what I did` IS A `What I did` @desc How you recorded it
GIVETH AN `Answer`
DECIDE `Can I meet the recording requirement electronically` IS
    `Answer the section` `the requirement`
        (    `what I did`'s `it was reasonable to expect the information to stay readily accessible for later reference`
         AND `what I did`'s `any data storage device the regulations require was used`)

-- s 12(2): a requirement "to retain, for a particular period, a document that is in the form of paper" is met "if the
-- person retains an electronic form of the document throughout that period, where: (a)" the method of generating it
-- reliably assured integrity; "(b)" readily accessible; "(c)" any regulation data-storage-device requirement met.
-- (No consent and no Commonwealth-entity limb: retention is my own act.)
@export Can I keep a scan (an electronic form) instead of the paper document a Commonwealth law requires me to retain (s 12(2))?
GIVEN `the requirement` IS A `The requirement` @desc The requirement to retain a paper document
      `what I did` IS A `What I did` @desc How you made and kept the electronic form
      `I kept it for the whole period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you kept the electronic form throughout the required period
GIVETH AN `Answer`
DECIDE `Can I meet the retention requirement with an electronic form` IS
    `Answer the section` `the requirement`
        (    `I kept it for the whole period`
         AND `what I did`'s `the electronic form was made by a method that reliably assures the integrity of the information`
         AND `what I did`'s `it was reasonable to expect the information to stay readily accessible for later reference`
         AND `what I did`'s `any data storage device the regulations require was used`)

-- s 12(4): a requirement to retain "information that was the subject of an electronic communication" is met if it is
-- retained in electronic form throughout the period, where it is readily accessible, the method reliably assures
-- integrity, and "(c) ... such additional information ... as is sufficient to enable the identification of the following:
-- (i) the origin of the electronic communication; (ii) the destination ...; (iii) the time when the electronic
-- communication was sent; (iv) the time when the electronic communication was received", also accessible; and (e) any
-- regulation device requirement.
@export Can I meet a Commonwealth law's requirement to retain an email or other electronic communication by keeping it electronically (s 12(4))?
GIVEN `the requirement` IS A `The requirement` @desc The requirement to retain the communication
      `what I did` IS A `What I did` @desc How you kept it
      `I kept it for the whole period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you kept it throughout the required period
GIVETH AN `Answer`
DECIDE `Can I meet the retention requirement for an electronic communication` IS
    `Answer the section` `the requirement`
        (    `I kept it for the whole period`
         AND `what I did`'s `it was reasonable to expect the information to stay readily accessible for later reference`
         AND `what I did`'s `the electronic form was made by a method that reliably assures the integrity of the information`
         AND `what I did`'s `I also keep enough to identify its origin, destination and times sent and received`
         AND `what I did`'s `any data storage device the regulations require was used`)

§§ `ss 14, 14A -- when my electronic communication is sent and received`

-- One communication between me and the other party. Times are hours counted from a common starting point (for example
-- midnight on the day it was sent), as either party could read them off their systems.
DECLARE `My communication` HAS
    `the addressee and I agreed otherwise about dispatch and receipt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it left an information system under my control or my sender's` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it went to an electronic address the addressee designated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hour it reached the addressee's electronic address` IS A NUMBER
    `the addressee has become aware it was sent to that address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hour the addressee became aware it was sent there` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Dispatch` IS ONE OF
    `at the time the addressee and I agreed`
    `when it left my information system`
    `when the addressee received it, because it never left my information system`

-- s 14(1): "unless otherwise agreed between the originator and the addressee ..., the time of dispatch ... is: (a) the
-- time when the electronic communication leaves an information system under the control of the originator or of the party
-- who sent it on behalf of the originator; or (b) if the electronic communication has not left an information system under
-- the control of the originator ...--the time when the electronic communication is received by the addressee." (Note: (b)
-- covers parties exchanging messages "through the same information system".) s 15E(1) applies s 14 to contracts as well.
@export When is my electronic communication taken to have been sent (s 14)?
GIVEN `the communication` IS A `My communication` @desc The communication you sent
GIVETH A `Dispatch`
DECIDE `When is my communication dispatched` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the communication`'s `the addressee and I agreed otherwise about dispatch and receipt`
            THEN `at the time the addressee and I agreed`
        IF `the communication`'s `it left an information system under my control or my sender's`
            THEN `when it left my information system`
        OTHERWISE `when the addressee received it, because it never left my information system`

-- s 14A(1): "(a) the time of receipt ... is the time when the electronic communication becomes capable of being retrieved
-- by the addressee at an electronic address designated by the addressee; or (b) the time of receipt ... at another
-- electronic address of the addressee is the time when both: (i) the electronic communication has become capable of being
-- retrieved by the addressee at that address; and (ii) the addressee has become aware that the electronic communication
-- has been sent to that address." s 14A(2): "it is to be assumed that the electronic communication is capable of being
-- retrieved by the addressee when it reaches the addressee's electronic address."
-- Answer: the hour of receipt, or NOTHING where the parties' agreement governs or the addressee is not yet aware.
@export At what hour is my electronic communication taken to have been received (s 14A)? Nothing if your agreement governs or it is not yet received.
GIVEN `the communication` IS A `My communication` @desc The communication you sent
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `At what hour is my communication received` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the communication`'s `the addressee and I agreed otherwise about dispatch and receipt` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the communication`'s `it went to an electronic address the addressee designated`
            THEN JUST (`the communication`'s `hour it reached the addressee's electronic address`)
        IF (NOT `the communication`'s `the addressee has become aware it was sent to that address`) THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST (max (`the communication`'s `hour it reached the addressee's electronic address`)
                            (`the communication`'s `hour the addressee became aware it was sent there`))

§§ `s 15 -- am I bound by a communication sent in my name`

DECLARE `A communication in my name` HAS
    `the addressee and I agreed otherwise about attribution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I sent it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was sent with my authority` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Attribution` IS ONE OF
    `bound: I sent it, or it was sent with my authority`
    `not bound under s 15(1); agency law may still bind me for someone acting within actual or apparent authority`
    `our agreement about attribution governs`

-- s 15(1): "unless otherwise agreed between the purported originator and the addressee ..., the purported originator of
-- the electronic communication is bound by that communication only if the communication was sent by the purported
-- originator or with the authority of the purported originator." s 15(2): this does not affect the law attributing conduct
-- within "actual or apparent authority".
@export Am I bound by an electronic communication sent in my name (s 15)?
GIVEN `the communication` IS A `A communication in my name` @desc The communication sent in your name
GIVETH AN `Attribution`
DECIDE `Am I bound by a communication sent in my name` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the communication`'s `the addressee and I agreed otherwise about attribution`
            THEN `our agreement about attribution governs`
        IF `the communication`'s `I sent it` OR `the communication`'s `it was sent with my authority`
            THEN `bound: I sent it, or it was sent with my authority`
        OTHERWISE `not bound under s 15(1); agency law may still bind me for someone acting within actual or apparent authority`

§§ `Part 2A -- contracts made electronically`

-- One contract, with the online proposal it started from and what happened when I ordered.
DECLARE `My contract` HAS
    `the proper law of the contract is the law of a State or Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that State or Territory has a law in terms substantially the same as Part 2A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was formed before Part 2A commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proposal was addressed to one or more specific parties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proposal was generally accessible to people using information systems` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proposal clearly indicated an intention to be bound on acceptance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a natural person and made an input error` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was dealing with the other party's automated message system` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the system gave me an opportunity to correct the error` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I told the other party of the error as soon as possible after learning of it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have used or received material benefit or value from the goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 15A(2): "This Part applies to or in relation to a contract only if: (a) the proper law of the contract is (or would on
-- its formation be) the law of a State or Territory; and (b) at the time the contract is formed, there is no law of that
-- State or Territory in terms substantially the same as this Part." s 17(3): "Part 2A do[es] not apply in relation to
-- contracts formed before the commencement date" (22 June 2011, from the endnotes). Whether a State law is "substantially
-- the same" is asked as a fact. (WA's Electronic Transactions Act 2011 has its own invitation-to-treat, automated-system
-- and input-error provisions, by its table of contents; whether they are "substantially the same" is not decided here.)
@export Does Part 2A of the Commonwealth Act apply to my contract at all (s 15A(2))?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A `My contract` @desc Your contract
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does Part 2A apply to my contract` IF
        `the contract`'s `the proper law of the contract is the law of a State or Territory`
    AND (NOT `the contract`'s `that State or Territory has a law in terms substantially the same as Part 2A`)
    AND (NOT `the contract`'s `it was formed before Part 2A commenced`)

DECLARE `Proposal` IS ONE OF
    `Part 2A does not apply to this contract`
    `an invitation to make offers: my order is the offer`
    `an offer: my acceptance can form the contract`

-- s 15B(1): a proposal "made through one or more electronic communications that: (a) is not addressed to one or more
-- specific parties; and (b) is generally accessible to parties making use of information systems; is to be considered as
-- an invitation to make offers, unless it clearly indicates the intention of the party making the proposal to be bound in
-- case of acceptance." (2): this "extends to proposals that make use of interactive applications for the placement of
-- orders". (A web shop's listing with a "Buy" button is an invitation to treat unless it clearly says otherwise.)
@export Is a website's proposal an offer I can accept, or only an invitation for me to make an offer (s 15B)?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A `My contract` @desc The contract and the online proposal it started from
GIVETH A `Proposal`
DECIDE `Is the online proposal an offer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `Does Part 2A apply to my contract` `the contract`) THEN `Part 2A does not apply to this contract`
        IF (NOT `the contract`'s `the proposal was addressed to one or more specific parties`)
           AND `the contract`'s `the proposal was generally accessible to people using information systems`
           AND (NOT `the contract`'s `the proposal clearly indicated an intention to be bound on acceptance`)
            THEN `an invitation to make offers: my order is the offer`
        OTHERWISE `an offer: my acceptance can form the contract`

-- s 15C: a contract formed by "(a) the interaction of an automated message system and a natural person; or (b) the
-- interaction of automated message systems; is not invalid, void or unenforceable on the sole ground that no natural
-- person reviewed or intervened in each of the individual actions ... or the resulting contract."
-- (FALSE here means only that this Act gives no such protection, because Part 2A does not apply; the State law may.)
@export Does s 15C protect my contract made with an automated system from being attacked on the sole ground that no person reviewed it?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A `My contract` @desc Your contract
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does s 15C protect my automated contract` IF
    `Does Part 2A apply to my contract` `the contract`

DECLARE `Input error` IS ONE OF
    `Part 2A does not apply to this contract`
    `no right: there was no input error with an automated system`
    `no right: the system let me correct the error`
    `no right: I did not tell the other party as soon as possible`
    `no right: I have had material benefit from the goods or services`
    `I may withdraw the part with the error, but that alone does not end the contract`

-- s 15D(2): "If: (a) a natural person makes an input error in an electronic communication exchanged with the automated
-- message system of another party; and (b) the automated message system does not provide the person with an opportunity
-- to correct the error; the person ... has the right to withdraw the portion of the electronic communication in which the
-- input error was made if: (c) the person ... notifies the other party of the error as soon as possible after having
-- learned of the error ...; and (d) the person ... has not used or received any material benefit or value from the goods
-- or services". (3): "The right of withdrawal ... is not of itself a right to rescind or otherwise terminate a contract."
@export Can I withdraw the part of my online order in which I made a typing (input) error (s 15D)?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A `My contract` @desc The contract and what happened with the error
GIVETH AN `Input error`
DECIDE `Can I withdraw my input error` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `Does Part 2A apply to my contract` `the contract`) THEN `Part 2A does not apply to this contract`
        IF (NOT `the contract`'s `I am a natural person and made an input error`)
           OR (NOT `the contract`'s `I was dealing with the other party's automated message system`)
            THEN `no right: there was no input error with an automated system`
        IF `the contract`'s `the system gave me an opportunity to correct the error`
            THEN `no right: the system let me correct the error`
        IF (NOT `the contract`'s `I told the other party of the error as soon as possible after learning of it`)
            THEN `no right: I did not tell the other party as soon as possible`
        IF `the contract`'s `I have used or received material benefit or value from the goods or services`
            THEN `no right: I have had material benefit from the goods or services`
        OTHERWISE `I may withdraw the part with the error, but that alone does not end the contract`
